  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing cooperative conservation of key Protected Areas in Perus Selva Central,..Yanachaga-Chemilln National Park and the Yanesha Communal Reserve</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen the management and conservation of the Communal Reserve, National Park, and its buffer zones by implementing field activities and conducting workshops with park guards from the Servicio Nacional de Areas Protegidas (SERNANP), volunteer Communal Rangers from the Asociacin para el Manejo de la Reserva Comunal Yanesha (AMARCY), and local residents to reduce illegal encroachments and resource overexploitation of wild resources in the Reserve and neighboring community lands, and threats related to climate change. Training also will be provided regarding hunting and forestry regulations developed previously in a collaborative process, and preparing educational materials about the regulations that the Rangers will explain and disseminate in their communities and annexes in the buffer zone of the Reserve.</narrative>
  </description>
